   "notes": "Pressure was calculated by the authors from the Pt volume using the Sokolova et al. (2016) Pt EOS. The published Pt differential stress t and KCl St diagnostic are retained. At high temperature, t was calculated using the Pt elastic-anisotropy factor at 300 K, as stated in the Table S1 footnote. This transcription follows the row alignment in the official MSA XLSX deposit; an earlier transcription from the split accepted-manuscript table incorrectly paired the Pt and KCl halves for runs 3 and 4. The October 2026 audit also corrects the Pt lattice/volume column permutation in runs 3/4 against the official workbook; every changed field is recorded in datasets/kcl_variant_sources/manifest.json. P, T, KCl volume and stress diagnostics are retained.",
